%I A401750 #30 Nov 19 2026 23:02:20
%S A401750 0,1,1,1,2,1,2,2,2,2,1,3,2,3,1,2,2,3,3,2,2,1,3,2,2,2,3,1,3,2,3,7,7,3,
%T A401750 2,3,1,4,2,2,2,2,2,4,1,2,2,4,5,5,5,5,4,2,2,1,3,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,3,1,3,2,
%U A401750 3,6,6,4,4,6,6,3,2,3,1,4,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,2,4,1
%N A401750 Table read by antidiagonals: T(n, k) is the height h of the shortest building which can see exactly h buildings due north and due west of itself, by rules in A400000.
%C A401750 An analog of A400000 for buildings on a two-dimensional grid.
%H A401750 Žiga Pirc, <a href="/A401750/b401750.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..9870</a>
%H A401750 MathOverflow, <a href="https://mathoverflow.net/questions/516465/2-dim-city-building-sequence">2-dim city-building sequence</a>.
%H A401750 Žiga Pirc, <a href="/A401750/a401750.cpp.txt">C++ program used for the b-file</a>.
%F A401750 T(n, k) = T(k, n).
%F A401750 T(n, 1) = A400000(n).
%F A401750 T(n, 2) = T(n, 3) = A400000(n) + 1.
%F A401750 T(n,k) = A402009(A000070(n+k-3)+A000070(k-2)) for n >= k >= 1. - _Pontus von Brömssen_, Nov 18 2026
%e A401750 Table starts:
%e A401750   0, 1, 1, 2, 1, 2, 1, 3, 1, 2 ...
%e A401750   1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 3, 2, 4, 2, 3 ...
%e A401750   1, 2, 2, 3, 2, 3, 2, 4, 2, 3 ...
%e A401750   2, 3, 3, 2, 7, 2, 5, 2, 6, 2 ...
%e A401750   1, 2, 2, 7, 2, 5, 2, 6, 2, 5 ...
%e A401750   2, 3, 3, 2, 5, 2, 4, 2, 5, 2 ...
%e A401750   1, 2, 2, 5, 2, 4, 2, 5, 2, 4 ...
%e A401750   3, 4, 4, 2, 6, 2, 5, 2, 6, 2 ...
%e A401750   1, 2, 2, 6, 2, 5, 2, 6, 2, 5 ...
%e A401750   2, 3, 3, 2, 5, 2, 4, 2, 5, 2 ...
%e A401750   ...
%e A401750 T(4, 5) is 7, since:
%e A401750   At height 0 it would see 2 buildings: (3, 5) and (4, 4).
%e A401750   At height 1 it would see 3 buildings: (3, 5), (4, 4), and (4, 3).
%e A401750   At height 2 it would see 4 buildings: (3, 5), (4, 4), (4, 3), and (2, 5).
%e A401750   At height 3 it would see 5 buildings.
%e A401750   At height 4 it would see 6 buildings.
%e A401750   At height 5 it would see 6 buildings.
%e A401750   At height 6 it would see 7 buildings.
%e A401750   At height 7 it would see 7 other buildings, so T(4, 5) = 7.
%o A401750 (C++) // See links section.
%Y A401750 Cf. A000070, A400000, A402009.
%K A401750 nonn,tabl,new
